# ---- Build / test artifacts ----
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Output of the go coverage tool
*.out
coverage.txt
cover.out
cover.html

# CPU / memory / block / mutex profile outputs
*.prof
cpu.prof
mem.prof
block.prof
mutex.prof

# Dependency directories (uncomment to vendor)
# vendor/

# Go workspace files
go.work
go.work.sum

# ---- Secrets / env ----
.env
.env.*

# ---- IDE / editor ----
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.\#*
\#*\#

# ---- OS noise ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---- Local session scratch (Claude Code) ----
# `.claude/` holds project-scoped AI rules and per-conversation memory
# (memory, settings.local.json, .remember/...). None of this is part
# of the library the user ships; it's our local working environment.
# `docs/superpowers/` holds design specs + implementation plans from
# brainstorming sessions; they're useful in-tree for the author but
# not part of the published package surface.
.claude/
docs/superpowers/

# --- Profiling artifacts (see PROFILING.md) ---
.profile/
